# migrations.manifest
#
# Byte-identical record of every MIGRATIONS entry (system / main DB) that
# has ever shipped. Format: <version>: <description>   (blank lines and #
# comments ignored).
#
# RULES (enforced by migrations_obey_append_only_manifest test):
#   1. Lines below this header are APPEND-ONLY. Never edit, never reorder,
#      never remove a line that has already shipped.
#   2. To add a new main migration: append a new (version, description)
#      line at the END here AND add the matching Migration entry at the end
#      of MIGRATIONS in migrations.rs. Both files must move together in
#      the same commit.
#   3. To change behavior for an already-published version, add a NEW
#      migration with the next higher version number; do NOT edit the old
#      entry. The runner records the version in schema_version; changing
#      a body for an already-applied version silently NO-OPs on every
#      existing deployment.
#
# History (2026-05-22, Patch 20): introduced after a recurrence-class bug
# in the TENANT_MIGRATIONS chain (v48 reaffected at upstream merge). The
# same risk applies to MIGRATIONS at every future upstream rebase: a
# concurrent definition of any v48..v63 by Ghost-Frame would silently
# diverge from VOCSAP deployments on the next merge. The test gives the
# diverge a CI-time error instead of a production schema drift.

